1. WHAT YOU MAY DO WITHOUT A LICENCE
------------------------------------

You may, free of charge and without asking permission:

  a) read, compile and run the Software for evaluation, learning, research and
     personal non-commercial use;
  b) modify the Software for those purposes, and keep your modifications
     private;
  c) use the Software on photographs you own or are authorised to edit, for
     evaluation output only — see clause 3 for commercial delivery;
  d) copy the Software for backup and archival purposes.


2. WHAT REQUIRES A COMMERCIAL LICENCE
-------------------------------------

A paid licence is required to:

  a) use the Software to produce images that are delivered to a client, sold,
     published commercially or used to promote a business;
  b) use the Software in a studio, agency, media organisation, club or any other
     commercial setting, including internal commercial workflows;
  c) redistribute the Software, in whole or in part, with or without
     modification;
  d) offer the Software, or a service substantially based on it, to third
     parties — hosted, embedded or otherwise.

Licences are perpetual per seat, with an optional annual support and update
plan. Seat counts, tiers and expiry are encoded in the signed key issued at
purchase and are verified offline by the application.


3. PHOTOGRAPHS AND DATA
-----------------------

  a) You retain all rights in your photographs. This agreement grants Kestrel
     Imaging no rights in your images.
  b) The Software processes images locally on your machine. It does not upload
     them, and it contains no telemetry.
  c) The Software does not train any model on your photographs. The optional
     personalisation feature stores bounded numeric preferences derived from
     your own feedback, on your own machine, and only with your explicit
     consent.
  d) You are responsible for holding the rights necessary to edit the images
     you process.


